        "description": "## Get Moods\n\nThis endpoint retrieves a list of moods available in the system.\n\n### Request\n\n- **Method**: `GET`\n    \n- **Endpoint**: `{{base_url}}/moods/`\n    \n\n### Response\n\n- **Status Code**: `200 OK`\n    \n- **Content-Type**: `application/json`\n    \n- **Response Body**: An array of mood objects, where each object contains the following keys:\n    \n    - `id`: A unique identifier for the mood.\n        \n    - `name`: The name of the mood.\n        \n    - `emoji`: An emoji representation of the mood.\n        \n    - `category`: The category to which the mood belongs.\n        \n\n### Example Response\n\n``` json\n[\n    {\n        \"id\": \"cc492bd4-30c9-470f-92f5-4bfc9ed525ad\",\n        \"name\": \"Calm\",\n        \"emoji\": \"😌\",\n        \"category\": \"Neutral\"\n    }\n]\n\n ```\n\nThis response format allows frontend to easily understand and utilize the available moods in their applications."
      },
