      "name": "auth",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "description": "## API Endpoint: User Authentication\n\n### Method\n\n`POST`\n\n### URL\n\n`{{base_url}}/auth/`\n\n### Description\n\nThis endpoint is used for user authentication. It allows clients to authenticate users by sending their credentials. Upon successful authentication, the server responds with user details and a token for session management.\n\n### Request Parameters\n\nThe request body must be sent in JSON format and should include the following parameters:\n\n- `username` (string): The username of the user attempting to authenticate.\n    \n- `password` (string): The password associated with the given username.\n    \n\n### Expected Response\n\nOn successful authentication, the server will respond with a JSON object containing the following fields:\n\n- `user_id` (string): The unique identifier for the authenticated user.\n    \n- `username` (string|null): The username of the authenticated user, or null if not applicable.\n    \n- `reset_token` (string): A token for password reset, if applicable.\n    \n- `is_guest` (boolean): Indicates whether the user is a guest (true) or a registered user (false).\n    \n- `date_joined` (string): The date and time when the user joined.\n    \n- `token` (string): A session token that can be used for subsequent authenticated requests.\n    \n\n### Example Response\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"user_id\": \"\",\n  \"username\": null,\n  \"reset_token\": \"\",\n  \"is_guest\": true,\n  \"date_joined\": \"\",\n  \"token\": \"\"\n}\n\n ```\n\nThis response structure allows clients to manage user sessions and understand the authentication status of the user.\n\nThis endpoint is used to authenticate users and initiate a session.\n\n### Request\n\n- **Method:** POST\n    \n- **Endpoint:** `{{base_url}}/auth/`\n    \n\n### Request Body Parameters\n\nThe request body should contain the following parameters:\n\n- **user_id** (string): The unique identifier for the user.\n    \n- **username** (string): The username of the user.\n    \n- **reset_token** (string): A token used for password reset.\n    \n- **is_guest** (boolean): Indicates whether the user is a guest.\n    \n- **date_joined** (string): The date when the user joined.\n    \n\n### Response\n\nUpon a successful request, the server will respond with a JSON object containing the following fields:\n\n- **user_id**: The unique identifier for the authenticated user.\n    \n- **username**: The username of the authenticated user or null if not applicable.\n    \n- **reset_token**: A token for resetting the password, which may be empty.\n    \n- **is_guest**: A boolean indicating if the user is a guest.\n    \n- **date_joined**: The date when the user joined, which may be empty.\n    \n\n### Expected Response Format\n\nThe response will be in JSON format, structured as follows:\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"user_id\": \"\",\n  \"username\": null,\n  \"reset_token\": \"\",\n  \"is_guest\": true,\n  \"date_joined\": \"\",\n  \"token\": \"\"\n}\n\n ```\n\nThis structure allows clients to easily understand the authentication status and details of the user."
      },
