      "name": "reset-token",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "description": "## Reset Token Endpoint\n\nThis endpoint is used to reset a user's authentication token. It allows clients to submit a reset token, which is typically used in scenarios such as password recovery or token refresh.\n\n### Request\n\n- **Method**: POST\n    \n- **URL**: `{{base_url}}/auth/reset-token/`\n    \n\n#### Request Body\n\nThe request body must be in JSON format and should include the following parameter:\n\n- **reset_token** (string): The token that is used to verify the reset request. This token should be securely generated and provided to the user through a previous step in the authentication process.\n    \n\n**Example Request Body:**\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"reset_token\": \"870356\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n### Response\n\nUpon successful processing of the request, the server will respond with a JSON object containing the following fields:\n\n- **message** (string): A message indicating the result of the request (can be empty).\n    \n- **token** (string): The new authentication token generated for the user.\n    \n- **user_id** (string): The unique identifier of the user associated with the token.\n    \n\n**Example Response:**\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"message\": \"\",\n  \"token\": \"\",\n  \"user_id\": \"\"\n}\n\n ```\n\n### Notes\n\n- Ensure that the reset token is valid and has not expired before making the request.\n    \n- The response will provide the new token, which should be used for subsequent authenticated requests."
      },
